2026-10-25|Sum of Beauty of All Substrings

Question:

Given a string s, return the sum of the beauty values of all its substrings.

Approach:

1. Start at each index i, treating it as the beginning of a substring.
2. Create a frequency array of size 26 to count lowercase English letters.
3. Extend the substring one character at a time, moving the ending index j from i to the end of the string.
4. Update the frequency of s[j].
5. Find the maximum and minimum non-zero character frequencies in the current substring.
6. Calculate the beauty as maximum frequency minus minimum frequency.
7. Add this beauty to the total sum.
8. Return the total after considering all substrings.

Solution:

```
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

class Solution {
public:
    int beautySum(string s) {
        int n = s.size();
        int totalBeauty = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int freq[26] = {0};

            for (int j = i; j < n; j++) {
                freq[s[j] - 'a']++;

                int maxFreq = 0;
                int minFreq = INT_MAX;

                for (int k = 0; k < 26; k++) {
                    if (freq[k] > 0) {
                        maxFreq = max(maxFreq, freq[k]);
                        minFreq = min(minFreq, freq[k]);
                    }
                }

                totalBeauty += maxFreq - minFreq;
            }
        }

        return totalBeauty;
    }
};
```

Time Complexity: O(n² × 26), which simplifies to O(n²) because the alphabet size is fixed.

Space Complexity: O(1), because the frequency array always contains 26 entries.
